From 7de07a0542a442c65f294775c6323dfa3b10abc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(network): complete RakNet disconnect lifecycle

RakNet emits a disconnect reason before closing its application pipeline.
Treat that event as an already initiated disconnect so the core close handler
does not start another handshake against a session in DISCONNECTING state.

A direct Java 26.3 connection to Bedrock 1.26.51.1 (protocol 2193) stays
active after the peer goes silent: the session detects its 30-second timeout,
but the repeated disconnect never completes. This affects the shared handler
used by direct connections and ViaProxy. Local closes still send one orderly
disconnect, and transport events continue to downstream handlers.

Discard inbound application packets once the application closes the
session or the transport reports a disconnect. The batch codec now emits
one packet per decode call and stops once the session is closed: a
Disconnect handled synchronously can close the channel while the rest of
its batch is still being split. RakNet keeps delivering
ordered datagrams that were already in flight, and ViaVersion stops
translating when the channel closes. On a live Bedrock 1.26.60 server
(protocol 2225), a Disconnect was followed 4 ms later by 15 queued packets.
They reached the Java decoder untranslated: a Bedrock PlayerList (ID 63)
decoded as a Java pong response, followed by 14 more decoder errors. The
native client also stops handling a session after it disconnects. Packets
read before the close still pass through unchanged, and each new
connection uses a new handler.

Embedded transport tests cover every RakNet reason, local close completion,
packets that arrive while RakNet finishes or after a transport
disconnect, and packets after a Disconnect in the same batch.
The resolved Cloudburst and VFP runtime session codecs both emit the event
before closing; no runtime-library reflection or client workaround is needed.

Declare the Cloudburst repository and RakNet compile/test dependency
explicitly after upstream removes its unused transport dependencies.
This handler still consumes the transport disconnect reason enum.
The same repository supplies later independently maintained signaling
code; its build prerequisite is recorded in the patch series.
